---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<section id="code">
  <h2>Get started</h2>

  <h3>Napari plugin</h3>
  <p>The <a href="https://github.com/ucsdmanorlab/napari-bootstrapper" target="_blank" rel="noopener">napari-bootstrapper</a> plugin provides an interactive graphical interface for applying the 2D&rarr;3D method to small volumes. Create sparse annotations directly in napari, generate dense volumetric segmentations, and perform basic proofreading and post-processing. Works with foundation models and the napari plugin ecosystem.</p>

  <pre><code>pip install napari-bootstrapper</code></pre>

  <figure class="no-frame no-invert">
    <video id="napari-video" autoplay loop muted playsinline width="1092" height="614"
           src={`${base}/napari.mp4`} poster={`${base}/posters/napari.webp`}
           aria-label="Napari bootstrapper plugin demonstration showing annotation, training, inference, and 3D segmentation output."
           style="width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 6px; display: block;">
    </video>
    <script is:inline>
      const v = document.getElementById('napari-video');
      const motion = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
      v.autoplay = !motion.matches;
      motion.addEventListener('change', () => {
        v.autoplay = !motion.matches;
        if (motion.matches) {
          v.pause();
          v.currentTime = 0;
        } else {
          v.play().catch(() => {});
        }
      });
    </script>
    <figcaption>Napari-bootstrapper plugin: annotate, train, infer, and export dense 3D segmentations within a single GUI.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h3>Bootstrapper CLI</h3>
  <p>The framework is open-source. It includes modules, scripts, and a command line interface for all components of the workflow: data preparation, 2D&rarr;3D models, LSD models, training pipelines, blockwise parallel inference and post-processing, evaluation, and error identification. Designed to scale to large volumes using lightweight distributed algorithms that do not require high-performance computing clusters.</p>

  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/ucsdmanorlab/bootstrapper.git
cd bootstrapper &amp;&amp; uv sync --locked</code></pre>

  <h3>Links</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/ucsdmanorlab/bootstrapper" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ucsdmanorlab/bootstrapper</a>: Full pipeline (CLI, training, inference, evaluation)</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/ucsdmanorlab/napari-bootstrapper" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ucsdmanorlab/napari-bootstrapper</a>: Napari plugin for interactive 2D&rarr;3D</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/funkelab/gunpowder" target="_blank" rel="noopener">funkelab/gunpowder</a>: Data loading and augmentation</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/funkelab/lsd" target="_blank" rel="noopener">funkelab/lsd</a>: Local Shape Descriptors</li>
  </ul>
</section>
